**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.ItemsPanelModelTests`

**How to implement.** The Items panel's state and `AddItem`, as semantic messages of the constructor window (001 §O 'Items panel: the list, "Add item from library model…"'; 001 §P `AddItem`; the S7.2 brief: a picker over presets, samples and item models, writes through KitProxy; the S7.1 mapper's request: offer `AppContext.itemModels` and the presets and sample versions as `ItemModelChoice`, mint the `ItemId` through an injected provider, send AddItem through `ItemDraft.addTo` and record through `KitLibraryContext.recordItem`; .spec-md §4 'UI'). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs`, beside `ClockProvider.system` (step 150): `type ItemIdProvider with static member system : ItemIdProvider` mints `ItemId (Guid.NewGuid ())` at each call (step 236), documented in one line citing spec 0050 S7.2. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S7.2. (a) Before the model: `AddItemForm = { itemId : ItemId; offers : ItemModelChoice list; chosenOpt : ItemModelChoice option; labelText : ControlCaption; dial : ItemDial }`: the open form, holding the new item's id, minted when the form opens; the models offered (step 216); the one chosen; the label as typed, a raw caption until `ItemLabel.tryCreate` reads it; and the dial. `member this.itemDraftOpt : ItemDraft option` is `Some { id = itemId; label = <it>; model = <the chosen>; dial = dial }` when a model is chosen and `ItemLabel.tryCreate labelText.value` answers `Ok`, and `None` otherwise. (b) `TableAndElementRotationModel` gains, after `flowStep` (step 238), each documented in one line: `itemModels : ItemModelProxy` (the item-model store the form offers, step 209), `itemIds : ItemIdProvider`, `selectedItemOpt : ItemId option` (the item the panel shows) and `addItemFormOpt : AddItemForm option`. `initWith` sets them to `ItemModelProxy.createInMemory ()`, `ItemIdProvider.system`, `None` and `None`. `DefaultStores.DefaultStoreSet` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:430`) gains `itemModels`, the `itemModels` of the in-memory stores it imports the Built-in catalogue into (steps 42, 94, 210), and `initTableAndElementRotation` and `initMain` set it by record update beside `sources` and `catalogueImports` (step 101), so the test scenes offer the eight built-in item models. (c) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains, each documented in one line: `SelectKitItem of ItemId` (a press of an item row), `OpenAddItemForm` (Add item from library model…), `ChooseNewItemModel of ItemModelChoice`, `SetNewItemLabel of ControlCaption`, `SetNewItemDial of ItemDial`, `CancelAddItemForm` and `AddItem of ItemDraft` (001 §P: the form's Add, and how a test adds an item). (d) Arms. `OpenAddItemForm` reads the offers in this order: the standalone forms from `model.itemModels.listItemModels ()` as `LibraryModelChoice`s; sourceModel, polarizerModel and sampleModel MUST be the resolved SourcePresetItemModel, IdealPolarizerItemModel and StackSampleItemModel versions from that same list, joined to their typed physics offers; the source presets of `model.library.entriesForKind LightSource` (each `SourceItem s` as `SourcePresetChoice (sourceModel, s)`); the polarizer presets of `entriesForKind LinearPolarizer` then `CircularPolarizer` (each `PolarizerItem p` as `PolarizerPresetChoice (polarizerModel, p)`, one per entry id); and the samples of `entriesForKind Sample` (each `SampleItem s` as `StackSampleChoice (sampleModel, SampleVersionId.firstOf s.id, s)`, the version an experiment's binding pins, `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:descriptorBinding`, so an item and an experiment name one entry). A library listing that fails offers nothing of its kind, as `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:allowedEntryIds` treats one; an `Error e` of the item-model store sets `kitStatus` to `The item models could not be listed — <e.describe>` and the other offers stay. The form opens with `itemId = model.itemIds.mintItemId ()`, those offers, nothing chosen, an empty label and `FixedMounting`. `SelectKitItem id` sets `selectedItemOpt = Some id` when `kitItems` holds the id, and changes nothing otherwise. `ChooseNewItemModel`, `SetNewItemLabel` and `SetNewItemDial` set the open form's field and change nothing without a form; `CancelAddItemForm` sets `addItemFormOpt = None`; none of these writes. `AddItem draft` is a write message: it goes through step 185's private read-only guard first, so a kit opened read-only answers `The kit is open read-only: nothing is saved.` and writes nothing. Otherwise `draft.addTo model.kitItems` (step 216): `Error e` sets `kitStatus` to `The item was not added — <e.describe>` and changes nothing else; `Ok item` is recorded through `{ kit = model.kit; imports = model.catalogueImports }.recordItem item` (step 219): `Ok ()` sets `kitItems` to the items with it in label order (ordinal), `selectedItemOpt = Some item.id`, `addItemFormOpt = None` and `kitStatus = None`; `Error e` keeps the items and sets `kitStatus` to `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>` (step 152's text). No remove, duplicate, template or other message is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/ItemsPanelModelTests.fs`, `module ItemsPanelModelTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment. Its models are `initMain ()` (the in-memory scratch kit over the Built-in stores, steps 150, 152) with `itemIds` a test-local provider answering fixed GUIDs in turn. `Add item from library model lists the item models, the presets and the samples, and mints the item's id`: `OpenAddItemForm` opens a form whose `itemId` is the provider's first GUID, nothing chosen, an empty label and `FixedMounting`, and whose offers are the eight `BuiltinCatalogue.itemModels ()` as `LibraryModelChoice`s ordered by name, then the source presets, then the polarizer presets, then the samples at version 1, in `entriesForKind`'s order. `the add form takes a model, a label and a dial, and Cancel closes it writing nothing`: `ChooseNewItemModel` of the circular-polarizer offer, `SetNewItemLabel (ControlCaption "CPL1")` and `SetNewItemDial (DialMounted DialPositive)` set the form, whose `itemDraftOpt` is that draft; with the label `  ` it is `None`; `CancelAddItemForm` closes the form, and `model.kit.proxy.readItems ()` answers `[]`. `AddItem records the item in the kit with its model's snapshot and selects it`: `AddItem` of the CPL1 draft leaves `kitItems` CPL1, CPL1 selected, the form closed and `kitStatus` `None`; `readItems ()` answers CPL1 and `listSnapshots ()` holds the circular polarizer's version 1 envelope. `AddItem of a label the kit holds is told and records nothing`: then `AddItem` of a draft labelled `cpl1` under a new id sets `kitStatus` containing `already has an item of that label`, and `kitItems` and `readItems ()` are unchanged. `a kit opened read-only adds no item`: over the model whose kit is its scratch kit's read-only view (`{ m.kit with proxy = m.kit.proxy.readOnlyView; access = ReadOnlyKitAccess }`, step 152's fixture), `AddItem` of the CPL1 draft sets `kitStatus` to the read-only text, and `readItems ()` answers `[]`. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.

**Acceptance.** After the panel's state lands, `OpenAddItemForm` MUST offer the item models, presets and samples with a minted id, and `AddItem` MUST record a new item through `recordItem`, refusing a label the kit holds and any write under a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `Add item from library model lists the item models, the presets and the samples, and mints the item's id`, `the add form takes a model, a label and a dial, and Cancel closes it writing nothing`, `AddItem records the item in the kit with its model's snapshot and selects it`, `AddItem of a label the kit holds is told and records nothing` and `a kit opened read-only adds no item`, the count rising by 5; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the fourteen s24 invariants MUST pass.
